sprites-hard 2026-11-25: despair.png: no web copy of the creature exists (source unknown). Re-cut from the video's own frame https://i.ytimg.com/vi/U67wZoy-1fE/maxres1.jpg (square at x316-515,y261-460, 200px): 3x Lanczos, alpha unmixed against the measured square colour (172,127,97) so the black silhouette keeps its own edge (no fading); white eyes kept opaque. 512px ~92% bottom-flush. Horizontal spike tips and tendril base touch the square edge in the video too.
sprites-s5 2026-11-27 (cm_s5): despair.png re-traced crisp (tools/art_s5_despair.py): same video-frame cut as above (https://i.ytimg.com/vi/U67wZoy-1fE/maxres1.jpg), alpha upsampled 4x, smoothed and thresholded to a hard silhouette with a 1-2 px anti-aliased edge (was a soft 3x upscale); eye arcs re-traced white; light gaps between the tendrils are transparent. Web search (Despair creature art, video description) found no original; maxresdefault.jpg shows it larger but with the horns out of frame. No edge fading.
